[00:01.40] On the way back home
[00:13.72] How long did it seem?
[00:24.18] Three days or four?
[00:35.16] Snow glazed all the trees
[00:45.86] My mother held me
[00:52.56] Like a motorcycle, so warm
[01:01.88] We sang melody
[01:20.18] Campin' out all night
[01:28.12] Slow moves in the light
[01:39.72] Of all the things that you've seen
[01:50.30] Was the motorcycle so warm you sang melody?
[02:28.34] At that moment I'd know
[02:37.48] Just how close we could be
[02:47.24] And though it always was mine
[03:00.64] It always seemed new to me
[03:12.68] Ten thousand colors in all
[03:23.02] Eyes like caves on my cheeks
[03:33.10] To all the people I've loved
[03:46.30] Don't think poor of me
[03:57.86] It wasn't 'til I woke up
[04:07.38] That I could hold down a joke or a job or a dream
[04:21.82] But then all three are one in the same
[04:35.12] And ALL then are one in the same
[04:47.58] And all us are one in the same
